    "result_text": "There's only one test class in the project, and the full suite is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `capacityWarning` following the existing `bulkSignupWarning` derived-field pattern. When an owner is created, the field is `true` if the owner's city (case-insensitive) already holds between 40 and 49 owners \u2014 approaching the hard limit of 50, which still rejects at 50.\n\nChanges:\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `capacityWarning` column, getter, and setter.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added a `CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 40` constant, a `computeCapacityWarning(city)` method (`count >= 40 && count < 50`, reusing the existing `countOwnersInCity`), and a call to set it in `populateDerivedFields` (a pre-save snapshot, so it never counts the new owner). The existing hard rejection in `requireCityHasCapacity` is untouched.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped `capacityWarning` onto the DTO.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `capacityWarning` schema property (drives DTO generation).\n- **`schema.sql`** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `capacity_warning BOOLEAN` column.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity` test and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1/1 tests green).",
